{
	"info": {
		"name": "Decidiq API Contract Suite",
		"description": "Newman/Postman API-contract tests for the Decidiq Nextcloud governance app. Locks the HTTP contract of decidiq's controllers (appinfo/routes.php + lib/Controller/*): meeting lifecycle, motion lifecycle, decision publication, the voting/quorum surface (open round / cast vote / tally / close), and settings. Meeting/decision/motion/voting-round CRUD is delegated to the OpenRegister object API (ADR-022); decidiq owns only the guarded governance endpoints. Every endpoint family is exercised for a happy path, an error/validation case (4xx not 500), and an authorization case (no auth -> 401). The suite is self-contained and idempotent: setup requests seed the prerequisite OpenRegister objects and teardown deletes everything created.\n\nAUTH MODEL: collection auth is noauth; every authenticated request carries an EXPLICIT basic-auth block (admin:admin via adminUser/adminPass) plus the 'OCS-APIRequest: true' header (NC app-framework controllers reject session-less POSTs without it as a CSRF failure). The no-auth requests carry NEITHER, and target {{noAuthBase}} (127.0.0.1) so the host-scoped NC session cookie established by authed localhost requests never leaks to them.\n\nPHASE-0 VOTING FIX LOCKED: tally returns a real, correct result (votesFor>votesAgainst => 'adopted') with no 500; cast creates a Vote with no 500; both error/validation paths return static-message 4xx, not 500.\n\nQUARANTINED REAL BUGS (asserted at their current status, NOT faked green — flip to happy-path when fixed):\n  (1) DecisionController::publish 500 on unknown id: find() raises OR's DoesNotExistException instead of returning null, so the controller's `=== null` 404 branch is unreachable and the exception escapes unhandled.\n  (2) Voting per-meeting chair guard / quorum participant resolution returns 403/cannot resolve for OpenRegister-object-API-created data: ParticipantResolver filters on '_relations.governance-body' but objects created via the standard OR object API store the link as a flat property ('governanceBody') or a flattened 'relations.0.*' map, neither of which is indexed under that relation-slug filter. open() (per-meeting chair check on the request-body meetingId) therefore 403s for seeded data. tally/close use the global chair fallback (admin) and DO work, which is how the tally contract is asserted live.\n\nUsage: see run-newman.sh. Pass collection variables baseUrl, noAuthBase, adminUser, adminPass.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "noAuthBase", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8080" },
		{ "key": "adminUser", "value": "admin" },
		{ "key": "adminPass", "value": "admin" },
		{ "key": "register", "value": "decidesk" },
		{ "key": "govBodyId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "participantId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "meetingId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "motionId", "value": "" },
